WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.620
In this 3-video series,

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:05.160
I show the science behind the
pros and cons of the flu vaccine,

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.253
pneumonia vaccine,
and shingles vaccine.

00:00:08.432 --> 00:00:14.668
"Benefits and Side Effects of the Flu Vaccine"

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.180
Every year,
influenza typically kills

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.420
between 4,000
and 20,000 Americans,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.080
though the death toll
for the 2017 to 2018 season

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.660
was estimated at 80,000,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.840
making it one of the deadliest
in the last half century.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.240
Most hospitalizations

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.760
and 90 percent
of flu-related mortality

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.220
occur in those
65 and older,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.740
and most over the age of 75.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.040
Mortality rates for the flu
at ages 75 and older

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.760
are 50 times higher
than those below age 65.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.280
Nonetheless,
the CDC recommends

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.440
everyone over the age
of 6 months

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.900
get a routine annual flu shot
every year,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.780
if for no other reason than
to help prevent transmission

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.460
to the more vulnerable.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.700
The cruel irony
is that older adults,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.560
the ones who need protection
the most,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.380
acquire less robust protection
from flu shots

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.960
due to waning immunity with age.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.240
Depending on the season,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.900
vaccination typically reduces
the risk of getting the flu

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.700
by about 40 to 50 percent.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.860
So, in healthy adults,

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.780
we can say
with moderate certainty

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.540
we can decrease the risk
of getting it

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.420
from like 2 percent each year
down to just under 1 percent.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.400
Among older adults,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.700
even if you get a similar
relative risk reduction,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.100
from 6 percent
down to 2.4 percent,

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.820
since the risk is higher
and the consequences greater,

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.340
the absolute benefits
are greater too.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.620
In the Northern Hemisphere,

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.680
the flu season can start
as early as September

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.660
and go as late as March.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.460
The problem
with getting vaccinated

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.020
too early in the season

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.680
is that immunity might wane
before the season is over,

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.540
especially in older adults.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:00.360
So, it might be good to wait
until October,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.760
but getting it at any time
throughout the season

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.640
is preferable to not getting
vaccinated at all.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.260
Yes, the influenza vaccine can
cause Guillain-Barré syndrome,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.120
an autoimmune attack
on your nerves

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.280
that can leave you paralyzed
for weeks,

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.800
but so too can getting the flu.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.740
There may be
1 to 2 additional cases

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.140
of Guillain-Barré
per million vaccinations

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.980
versus about 17 extra cases
per million contacts

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:26.880
with the flu virus.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.060
So, you're much more likely
to be temporarily paralyzed

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.220
by the flu than the flu shot,

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:36.240
but since it takes vaccinating
about 30 older people

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.920
to prevent one case of the flu,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.220
getting vaccinated
would still, in expectation,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.280
raise your overall
Guillain-Barré risk.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.680
But the reason flu shots
are recommended

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.980
is not to lower risk of some
obscure autoimmune syndrome

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.740
but to reduce the common,
and potentially devastating,

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.380
impacts of the flu
that extend well beyond

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.120
just the respiratory infection.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.720
In the week following
a confirmed flu infection,

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.700
the risk
of having a heart attack

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.200
shoots up six-fold.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.660
The inflammation of infection

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.540
can destabilize
atherosclerotic plaques,

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.380
constrict arteries,

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.240
and make the blood
more liable to clot.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.600
So, might flu vaccinations
save lives

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.860
in more ways than one?

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.140
That's why indirectly

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.720
the flu may kill
up to three times more.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.240
Those who get their flu shots

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.540
are indeed less likely to die
from cardiovascular disease

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.180
in a given year as well
as all causes put together.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:33.240
In other words, those who get
regular flu shots live,

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.220
on average, longer lives.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.580
But who disproportionally
gets flu shots?

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:43.980
White, married, nonsmokers
of a higher social class,

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.720
with higher education,
higher incomes,

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:46.260
and health insurance.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.020
You can't tell
if it's truly cause-and-effect

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.200
until you put it to the test.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.200
There have been four
randomized controlled trials,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.240
flu shots versus placebo shots,

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.880
in those with
pre-existing heart disease,

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.820
and overall,
those who got the real shots

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.640
had a 56 percent lower chance
of dying

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.020
from cardiovascular disease

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.800
and a 47 percent lower chance
of dying

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:11.940
from all causes put together.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.440
So, flu shots really can be
an extraordinary life-saver.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.320
Whether the observational data

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.360
showing fewer deaths
across the board,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.300
even among those without
pre-existing heart disease,

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.820
similarly pans out is,
as of yet, unknown,

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.640
but if you notice
for secondary prevention

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.380
the randomized
controlled trials

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.120
showed even more protection

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.280
than the observational studies
hinted at.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.920
Given the benefits,

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.640
overcoming vaccine hesitancy
should be as simple

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.580
as correcting misinformation,
but sadly,

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.600
debunking vaccine myths
may actually backfire.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.360
Busting the myth that
inactivated flu shots,

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.860
the type given to older adults,

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:54.060
can give you the flu

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.360
surprisingly makes people
even less likely to get it.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.300
Similarly,
correcting the falsehood

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.520
that MMR vaccines
cause autism

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.280
or that pertussis vaccination

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.920
causes as many side effects
as people think

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.820
paradoxically makes people
less inclined to vaccinate.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.960
The researchers conclude
"correcting vaccine myths

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.100
may not be an effective approach
to promoting vaccination."

